+# META GAMING runtime candidate
+
+This change compiles independent server-side adapters for
+`metagaming_normal_myr` and `metagaming_free_myr`. It does not enable either
+profile, publish a Play button, or record supplier acceptance.
+
+## Safety boundary
+
+- Normal and free-credit use different profile, player and ledger namespaces.
+- The account is derived from the compiled profile and is checked again by the
+  integration gateway. A browser cannot select credentials or an API origin.
+- Player/launch, wallet, recovery and report requests use four different peer
+  tokens. Aliased or malformed tokens reject the entire secret document.
+- All submission switches are false unless a server-side profile document
+  records merchant-contract evidence, session-closure evidence and an
+  authorized QA member or production acceptance.
+- Only English is implemented. The portal sends the gateway's reviewed `en`
+  value for provider English `en-us`. Customer returns require the exact
+  `https://www.master7.best` origin, and provider launch URLs require an exact
+  configured HTTPS origin.
+- Deposit and withdrawal responses do not contain transaction IDs. Their
+  result stays `unknown` until `CheckTransferStatus` returns the original
+  account-bound reference and exact amount.
+- `PullLog` has no requested-time-window coverage receipt. Pages therefore
+  remain `complete:false`; the adapter never calls `FlagLog` automatically.
+- The free-credit profile is executable for isolated protocol testing but is
+  rejected by the existing cash-ledger seeding gate.
+
+## Remaining external blockers
+
+The supplier must clear the current HTTP 403/allowlist response and confirm
+merchant amount semantics, issued-URL invalidation, late-result finality and
+report acknowledgement. Controlled QA and production evidence are still
+required before any capability can be enabled.
